patch type="fixed" "Region URLs returned by region discovery are now validated before the SDK fails over to them. Only encrypted (`wss`/`https`) LiveKit Cloud URLs without embedded credentials are accepted, and the check is enforced in `RegionInfo`'s initializer so it covers both sources of a region list: the `/settings/regions` response and the regions the server reports over signalling. Previously only the application-supplied URL was checked and the returned entries were used as they arrived, which matters because the SDK authenticates to those URLs with the participant token"
